--- title Applying a refinement only if a word says so
--- about `insert/:only` takes the refinement when ONLY is true and
--- about leaves it off when ONLY is false or none. Without it a
--- about function that passes its own refinements on has to branch,
--- about writing the call twice. Rebol's own COLLECT uses it, and so
--- about does much of the rest of its library.

--- id conditional-refinements/applied-when-the-word-is-true
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: copy []
only: true
insert/:only b [1 2]
mold b
--- result
"[[1 2]]"

--- id conditional-refinements/left-off-when-the-word-is-false
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
c: copy []
only: false
insert/:only c [1 2]
mold c
--- result
"[1 2]"

--- id conditional-refinements/left-off-when-the-word-is-nothing
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is the case that matters: an unasked refinement arrives
--- note as none, and passing it straight on has to mean "not asked".
--- code
d: copy []
only: none
insert/:only d [1 2]
mold d
--- result
"[1 2]"
